# process.nextTick(() => {}); Buffer.prototype.toJSON.call("ab").scan()
# Buffer.prototype.toJSON is written in JavaScript, and the table says of its result that it is an object and nothing more. Where the program holds that code Link sees what it makes: the row makes nothing of the host.
# If it counted as a row of the host that says nothing of what it hands out, objects of any class might exist: the call would find `scan` on the prototype object of the class of Bun.Glob,
# and the function of the library behind it would be in the program.
# The control: row-whose-code-the-program-does-not-hold-lets-any-class-exist.ir.
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK: function f2 unreached
# CHECK-NOT: function f4 unreached

